Description: Eclipse-based IDE for Event-B (release candidate)
 The Rodin platform is an Eclipse-based integrated development environment for
 Event-B. It supports refinement, mathematical proof, type-checking and the
 generation and discharge of proof obligations, and is extensible through a wide
 range of plug-ins.
 .
 This package tracks the newest eventb-rossi Rodin Bundle, release candidates
 included: Rodin 3.10 with parallel automatic proving, the SMT solvers, the ProB
 animator and disprover, the Proof Obligation Cleaner and the Rossi bridge. It
 is a drop-in replacement for the stable "rodin" package, with which it
 conflicts. It needs a Java 21 or newer runtime; webkit2gtk is recommended for
 the browser-backed views.
